@startuml sequence-digitalizer-labelling
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: sample once (CLI), then label (SPA), then export (CLI or API). The
'       sampler stratifies by language and by the decider's band, so the
'       unsure cases are included. Labellers never see the band. About 10 % of
'       items are offered to a second labeller for Cohen's kappa.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, three scenarios, proposed
'       (evilflowers-books-digitalizer#7).
' Source: evilflowers-books-digitalizer#7 (2026-11-16); EvilFlowersCatalog
'         develop 709b712 (extraction/admin_views.py regions with band,
'         graph/views.py chapters and related; read 2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Labelling for decider calibration: sample, label, export (proposed, 2026-11-16)

actor "Operator" as op
participant "SPA\nLabelling" as spa
participant "studio API /\nCLI" as api <<focus>>
database "studio DB" as pg
participant "Catalog dev\n/api/v1" as cat

== sample (CLI: studio sample-labels ~--task figure_kind ~--n 300) ==
api -> cat : GET entries?extraction_status=available (paged)
api -> cat : GET entries/{id}/extraction/regions?kind=figure
cat --> api : regions with band, p, decision
api -> api : strata language x band, fill quotas
api -> pg : insert label_items (payload for the screen,\nhidden: band, p, decision)

== label (SPA) ==
op -> spa : pick task, press 1..9 or s (skip)
spa -> api : GET labelling/tasks/{task}/next (X-Operator)
api -> pg : an item this labeller has not answered:\na second-labeller item while below 10 %, else a fresh one
api --> spa : item without any model answer
spa -> api : GET labelling/items/{id}/image
api -> cat : GET regions/{region_id}/image (Bearer)
spa -> api : POST labelling/items/{id}/labels {task, value}
api -> pg : upsert label (item, task, labeller)

== export (CLI: studio export-labels ~--task figure_kind) ==
api -> pg : labels of the task, skip excluded
api --> op : JSONL, one line per label;\nsummary: counts per label and language, kappa on doubly labelled items

caption Sections: chapters + related give the pairs; the text is the section's first paragraphs (no summary route yet).
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/sequence-digitalizer-labelling.puml
@enduml
